window.products.push({"id":625338,"name":"ZWILLING J.A. Henckel's Four Star 8 Piece Knife Block Set","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61W3Uh5cBDL._AC_SL1000_.jpg","description":"J.A. HENCKELS FOUR STAR series is one of the world's most popular knife lines. Four Star knives were designed and developed in close cooperation with renowned professional chefs. The result was a fully forged knife with a unique molded handle. First introduced in 1976, the Four Star range today is still one of the world's most popular knife series. The Four Star series contains knives for all tasks, including the following open stock knife types: pare, bread, peeling, sandwich, utility, carving, chef's, granton edge slicer, and others. The Four Star series features high impact polypropylene handles that are permanently bonded to the knife blades without any gaps. These comfortable, molded handles are break-proof, sanitary, and colorfast. In addition, the super bolster and full rat-tail tang provides weight, insures safety, and adds balance. Four Star knives are also available in a range of block sets and gift sets. The knives are made in Solingen, Germany. Lifetime Guarantee! Four Star knives are precision forged from a single piece of J.A. HENCKELS exclusive high-carbon, no-stain steel formula under the all-new SIGMAFORGE standard. As a result, Four Star knives have improved quality consistency, lasting sharpness, and perfect geometry. SIGMAFORGE one-piece construction also provides high precision and improved stability of the blade and steel structure, thus improving cutting-edge retention for lasting sharpness. In addition, Four Star knives use J.A. HENCKELS FRIODUR ice hardening for corrosion resistance, a process that also contributes to cutting-edge retention. For over 275 years, J.A. Henckels has been known worldwide for making the finest cutlery available in the marketplace. It was in Solingen, Germany in 1731, where knife maker Peter Henckels registered the \"twin\" symbol - now synonymous with quality knives - making it one of the oldest trademarks in the world. Over the years, Henckels has been at the forefront of cutlery innovations and technology.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61W3Uh5cBDL._AC_SL1000_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"ZWILLING","source_asin":"B011S6A7R0","category_path":"Home & Kitchen"},"sku":"BM-625338","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B011S6A7R0","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Home_and_Kitchen_2023.jsonl","source_asin":"B011S6A7R0","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
